# Issue #001 — Start Before You're Ready

**Monday, June 16, 2026 · Craft**

---

## Opening Thought

There's a version of this newsletter that I planned for six months. I had a Notion doc, a content calendar, a brand guide, a posting schedule. I had a logo in three sizes. I had every reason to keep planning.

Then I remembered something a photographer friend told me: *"The camera you have with you is the best camera."* Not the one on the wishlist. The one in your hand, today.

This first edition is that camera.

You're reading this because something in you wants to make things — and maybe because you've also been waiting for the right moment to start. I want to spend the next few hundred words making the case that the right moment is a myth, and that Monday morning is close enough.

The difference between people who make things and people who want to make things usually isn't talent, money, or connections. It's a willingness to produce something unfinished and let it be seen. Every creator I genuinely admire has a trail of awkward early work they're slightly embarrassed by. That trail is proof they showed up before they were ready.

So here's what I want for you this week: one small, real thing. Not the full project. One piece of it. A paragraph, a sketch, a single photo, a rough voice note. Something that exists in the world instead of only in the plan.

We'll build from there, every Monday.

