## The Gear Take

**Sony ZV-E10 II** ($700 body only)

For the creator who keeps telling themselves they'll start filming "when they have better gear" — this is the camera. It's a mirrorless with a full APS-C sensor, a flip-out touchscreen for solo shooting, and Sony's subject-tracking autofocus, which is genuinely good. No weather sealing, no 4K/60fps. Those are the tradeoffs that keep the price honest.

Pair it with the Sony 16-50mm kit lens to start, then a 35mm f/1.8 when you're ready to get serious about image quality. The ZV-E10 II won't be the camera you use forever. It'll be the camera that gets you started.

